 :caveats
 ["Counts are exact. Wall-clock is NOT measured -- multiply round trips by a measured
   per-GET RTT if you want an estimate, and say which RTT you used."
  "The 5000-doc cells are NOT a controlled comparison: the snapshot prolly-tree changed
   shape between the two runs (height 3 / widths [1 2 48] / 51 nodes -> height 2 /
   [1 48] / 49 nodes) for reasons unrelated to this change -- a prolly-tree pin moved.
   The 1000-doc and 20000-doc cells ARE controlled (identical height, widths and node
   counts across runs), so attribute the delta from those. :snapshot-half-controlled?
   records this per cell rather than leaving it to the reader to notice."
  "The (20000, 64) cell had no pre-change counterpart: the 2026-08-01 run stopped at
   6 of 7 cells. It is reported here without a :before."
  "This measures the LIBRARY at its west pin. It does NOT establish that the deployed
   kotobase.net worker carries the change -- see :deployment-status."
  "The novelty walk is still SEQUENTIAL: `novelty-cids` enumerates the chain with the
   sync get-fn, and a successor CID still only exists inside its predecessor. What
   changed is the length of that chain (n -> ceil(n/16)), not its nature."]

