 :follow-ups
 [{:target "kotoba-lang/kotobase-peer"
   :what "bench/kotobase_peer/dag_shape_bench.clj counts a novelty SEGMENT as one tx,
          because `novelty-shape` only knows the subject directory's \"entries\" key and
          not the queue's \"es\" key. Before the fix below, the 64-tx backlog reported
          :txs 4 while :novelty-count said 64 -- the hop count was right, the tx count
          was not, and a receipt that disagrees with itself invites the wrong reading.
          This session's numbers were produced WITH the patch applied."
   :status :not-upstreamed
   :why "No write access to kotoba-lang from this session."
   :patch "diff --git a/bench/kotobase_peer/dag_shape_bench.clj b/bench/kotobase_peer/dag_shape_bench.clj\nindex ac73cc9..07e98bd 100644\n--- a/bench/kotobase_peer/dag_shape_bench.clj\n+++ b/bench/kotobase_peer/dag_shape_bench.clj\n@@ -178,9 +178,16 @@\n                    (let [n (ipld/decode (get store c))]\n                      (recur (some-> (get n \"rest\") ipld/link-cid)\n                             (inc hops)\n-                            (+ txs (if (contains? n \"entries\")\n-                                     (count (get n \"entries\"))\n-                                     1)))))))\n+                            (+ txs (cond\n+                                     ;; the queue's 16-entry segment shape\n+                                     ;; (kotobase-peer c8e4f96) -- without this\n+                                     ;; branch a 64-tx backlog reads as 4 txs,\n+                                     ;; because each segment counts as one\n+                                     (contains? n \"es\") (count (get n \"es\"))\n+                                     ;; the subject directory's segment shape\n+                                     (contains? n \"entries\") (count (get n \"entries\"))\n+                                     ;; a pre-segment single-entry node\n+                                     :else 1)))))))\n         front (walk (some-> (get state \"novelty-front\") ipld/link-cid))\n         back (walk (some-> (get state \"novelty-back\") ipld/link-cid))\n         idx (walk (some-> (get state \"novelty-subject-index\") ipld/link-cid))]\n"}
  {:target "kotoba-lang/kotobase-protocols-worker"
   :what "src/kotobase_protocols_worker/kotobase_store.cljs's hydrate docstring still cites
          bench/results/2026-08-01-dag-shape.edn and says the novelty half 'is a cons chain
          and stays sequential under both'. Still true in kind, but the magnitude it implies
          (91-97% of hydrate) is now wrong."
   :status :not-upstreamed}
  {:target "network-awai/net-kotobase"
   :what "Confirm the deployed worker bundle carries c8e4f96, then re-measure the live
          p50. The 2,282ms hydration figure predates the change."
   :status :blocked-on-access}]

